{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.YoungDiagramKernelPincer"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.carrier_mem_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.carrier_mem_three","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L169-L238","doc":"**The depth-1 carrier is one of three cells**: `(0,0)`, `(0,1)` or `(1,0)`.\n\n`carrier_fst_or_snd_eq_zero` puts it on row 0 or column 0; pushing further out along either\naxis produces a *second* missed cell — `(0,1)` in the row case, `(1,0)` in the column case —\ncontradicting the singleton. These are exactly the carriers of the second-instance audit's three\nshapes: two-corner `(a,2,1^c)` at `(0,0)`, row `(n)` at `(0,1)`, column `(1^n)` at `(1,0)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.carrier_fst_or_snd_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.carrier_fst_or_snd_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L135-L167","doc":"**The carrier lies on the first row or the first column.** If both coordinates were positive\nthe hook would miss *two* distinct cells — the corner `(0,0)` and `(0, p.2)` — contradicting\n`card_sdiff_hookUnion_eq_one`. Combined with the corner lemma this is the case split that pins the\ndepth-1 carriers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.origin_not_mem_hookUnion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.origin_not_mem_hookUnion","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L122-L133","doc":"**The corner is outside every hook but its own.** The hook of `p` meets row `p.1` only from\ncolumn `p.2` rightward and column `p.2` only strictly below row `p.1`, so it contains `(0,0)`\nexactly when `p = (0,0)`. This is the pivot of the depth-1 case analysis: for any other carrier the\ncorner is *the* missed cell, which then forces every other cell into the hook. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.mem_legF_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.mem_legF_iff","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L111-L120","doc":"Membership in the strict leg, unfolded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.mem_armF_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.mem_armF_iff","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L100-L109","doc":"Membership in the arm, unfolded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.exists_unique_missed_cell","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.exists_unique_missed_cell","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L92-L96","doc":"The missed cell, named: at `hookLen = n − 1` there is exactly one cell outside the hook. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.card_sdiff_hookUnion_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.card_sdiff_hookUnion_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L84-L90","doc":"**At `hookLen = n − 1` the complement of the hook is a singleton.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.card_hookUnion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.card_hookUnion","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L61-L76","doc":"**The hook's cardinality**: `|arm ∪ strict leg| = hookLen`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.hookUnion_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.hookUnion_subset","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L57-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.armF_legF_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.armF_legF_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L48-L55","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.legF_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.legF_subset","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L40-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.armF_subset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.armF_subset","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L34-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.legF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.legF","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L30-L32","doc":"The **strict leg** of a cell: the cells strictly below it in the same column. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.armF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.HookArmLeg.armF","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/HookArmLeg.lean#L26-L28","doc":"The **arm** of a cell: the cells to its right in the same row. ","signatureChunk":0}]}